	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "AuXyEuLJzVWYTzPnD",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the reviewed package: ST 20, DX 12, IQ 2, HT 12, HP 20, WILL 9, PER 12, FP 12, SPEED 6, MOVE 5, DODGE 9, DR 1. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "AbwmCghWnBtczMxV3",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 41 (offense 27, protection 14), threat tier standard, appearing 2."
		},
		{
			"id": "Ak5lDfXV6Hd98D4EI",
			"text": "Implant (2d toxic), reach C: Female spider eaters lay their eggs inside paralyzed creatures of SM+2 or bigger. The eggs gestate for six weeks, then the host takes 2d toxic damage each hour for 13 cycles. This damage cannot be resisted. Once the host loses 1/2 of their HP to this effect, they begin experiencing terrible pain (p. B428) until they heal above that threshold. Once the host loses 2/3 of their HP to this effect, they begin experiencing agony (p. B428) until they heal above that threshold. The eggs can be removed with a successful Surgery roll (failure deals 1d-1 injury), or a Cure Disease spell cast at a -5 penalty. If the host dies to this effect, the young emerges, literally devouring the host from inside."
		},
		{
			"id": "A2A7k2fHGdhmEHU-m",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/spider-eater.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "Azun1atjNWxKaYCS2",
			"text": "Source template total: 126 points."
		},
		{
			"id": "AauQRIipnLBpQbfFo",
			"text": "Library-rebuilt template total: 126 points."
		},
		{
			"id": "ADgfNcNCTkwdktfhQ",
			"text": "CER was computed from parsed Typical Stats using the Dungeons On Automatic baseline CER path."
		},
		{
			"id": "A-p9aSWzOZCpVnG0w",
			"text": "Review attacks, special abilities, encounter frequency, treasure, grappling, and GCS modifiers before approval."
		},
		{
			"id": "AgD0VthHde60VH_aW",
			"text": "Size 7 hexes; Weight 4,000 lbs."
		},
